-- R42 - PRINTS AND CALENDAR
-- Source: thread "Upgrade Fable Takeaways from Opus gaps", owner's ask of 27 Nov 2026; month comparison 27 Oct to 27 Nov.
-- Proposed 27 Nov 2026 and put in force early by single-statement UPDATE the same day (print and input additions only). "revert R42" removes it.
-- Early in force: update dash.rules set status='in_force', decided_at=now(), apply_after=now() where rid='R42';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "PRINTS AND CALENDAR: every scheduled release since the last edition sent with actual vs consensus; a fixed 7-session radar with consensus and market-implied odds; JGB 10Y, Bund 10Y and HSI on the tape", "body": "PRINTS AND CALENDAR (owner's ask of 27 Nov 2026; from the month comparison of Fable with the Opus, Gemini and ChatGPT editions, 27 Oct to 27 Nov).\n\n1. PRINTS SINCE THE LAST EDITION. The window runs from the send time of the last Takeaways edition of this pipeline that was actually sent (up to four days back when mornings were missed) to the build. In it, list every scheduled release in the book's markets: US, euro area, Germany, France, Italy, Spain, UK, Japan, China, Korea, Taiwan, Australia, New Zealand, Canada, India, Indonesia, Singapore, Thailand, Philippines, Malaysia. Kinds: CPI, PPI, GDP, flash and final PMIs, labour, retail sales, trade, industrial output, central bank decisions, minutes, accounts and staff forecasts, and JGB, UST, Bund, KTB and other sovereign auctions (yield, cover). Each gets actual vs consensus vs prior and a one-word read (beat, miss, in line). The 06:00 to 07:15 SGT window (Australia, Japan, Korea prints) is re-checked at the late pickup. A print found by the sweep but not confirmed at a primary page by build time prints with \"[sweep, unconfirmed]\"; it is never held back. Any release that an earlier edition named as a test, kill or invalidation for a card, lean or question is always reported with its result, even after a missed morning. Place: a PRINTS sub-block at the end of THE LAST 24H, at most eight lines (minor prints grouped on one line); R33 may move minor lines to the overflow file, never a named test.\n\n2. RADAR. A fixed look-ahead of seven sessions for the same markets and kinds, plus liquidity operations (MLF, RRR effective dates, repo operations), finance-ministry intervention data releases, voters' scheduled speeches and US Treasury refunding or auction sizes. Every entry that a card, lean or question names carries consensus and prior (or \"cons n/a\"). Every central bank decision inside seven sessions carries a market-implied probability with its source and time (OIS, futures, Polymarket or Kalshi; \"implied n/a\" when none was found), refreshed every morning, never carried stale; a stale figure prints \"stale since <time>\".\n\n3. TAPE. JGB 10Y, Bund 10Y and HSI are always on the tape line, with their as-of date.\n\n4. FOOTER. \"Prints: <n> since <time> (<b> beat, <m> miss, <u> unconfirmed) · Radar: <n> entries, consensus on <c> of <k> named, implied on <i> of <d> decisions\".", "rationale": "Month comparison (project files fable_gap_review/): the second and third most frequent material Fable gaps were data prints (an Australian CPI the sweep found but held back as unverified, a German flash HICP never mentioned while the ECB lean stood, Australian jobs and US retail sales missed after mornings with no edition, prints in the 06:00 to 07:15 SGT window) and calendar holes (Japan GDP, the 40Y JGB auction, Korea and Indonesia CPI, the MoF intervention report, MLF maturities missing from the radar; consensus missing on the releases a lean depended on; central bank odds stale or absent). The prompts are at their byte cap, so this goes in as a rule.", "evidence": "Project files fable_gap_review/gaps_w1..w5.tsv and gaps_d27nov.tsv; summaries per week.", "revert_if": "Revert if the PRINTS and RADAR lines push the email over R33's budget on two mornings in a week, or the daily comparison finds the same kind of miss three times after it is in force.", "review_due": "2026-12-18", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
